  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\bigl(\\operatorname{Measure.count}\\restriction A\\bigr).\\mathrm{map}\\, f \\;=\\; c \\cdot \\bigl(\\operatorname{Measure.count}\\restriction T\\bigr),",
    "plain": "The parent entry (\"General Uniform Fiber Transfer\") proves, event by event, that an equal-fiber surjection preserves the uniform distribution — it transfers `uniformOn` on the domain to `uniformOn` on the codomain. This problem asks whether that fact can be lifted to the clean, structural statement about `MeasureTheory.Measure.map`: rather than checking each event, express the whole transfer as a single pushforward identity for `Measure.count` restricted to $A$ and $T$.",
