    "insights": [
      "The clean Measure.map pushforward identity requires MapsTo f A T (f maps A into T), NOT just the parent SurjOn: the global identity is tested on all measurable S, so any mass mapped outside T would break equality against c • count.restrict T.",
      "The whole Measure.map identity collapses onto the verified parent lemma uniform_fiber_count (ncard form) via a count=ncard bridge on finite sets; no new combinatorics.",
      "Proof shape: Measure.ext on S; Measure.map_apply + Measure.restrict_apply reduce LHS to count(f⁻¹S ∩ A) = count(A ∩ f⁻¹(S∩T)) [MapsTo], then count=ncard, then uniform_fiber_count gives c*(S∩T).ncard = c*count(S∩T) = RHS.",
      "VERIFICATION-READINESS AUDIT (researcher-5, build-independent): all 4 parent/grandparent lemma calls (uniform_fiber_count, surjOn_fiber_decomp, singleton_fiber_disjoint, ncard_biUnion_eq_of_uniform) match their AUTHORITATIVE signatures exactly by inspection. Resolved a genuine 2-signature ambiguity: BallotFiberTransfer.ncard_biUnion_eq_of_uniform binds to the explicit-arg/pointwise-disjoint version at BallotProblemOQ01OQ02OQ01.lean:46, and the 7 supplied args match it.",
      "Highest residual build risk = count_eq_ncard: it uses UNPRIMED Set.ncard_eq_toFinset_card (explicit s hs), but the verified corpus (…OQ01OQ02OQ01Aristotle.lean:19,51) only uses the PRIMED Set.ncard_eq_toFinset_card. Confirm the unprimed explicit-arg form exists and lands on the same hs.toFinset.card as Measure.count_apply_finite s hs."
    ],
